  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between bleomycin and G-protein coupled receptor 81, as all three paths indicate that bleomycin acts through palmarumycin CP18, which in turn targets the G-protein coupled receptor 81. The final scores from the three paths, though slightly varying, all point to a consistent pathway involving palmarumycin CP18 as a critical mediator. This implies that bleomycin may exert its effects by modulating the activity of G-protein coupled receptor 81, potentially through a mechanism involving receptor activation or signaling pathways. The shared involvement of palmarumycin CP18 across different cell lines (HT-144, MCF-10A, and SK-MEL3) supports the idea that this compound is a common mediator in the interaction between bleomycin and the receptor. The presence of a well-documented mode of action—through a target that is a G-protein coupled receptor—adds to the plausibility of this relationship. The evidence is consistent and does not suggest any contradictions or uncertainties in the mechanistic pathway.",
